From: Alp Lab AB
Subject: [PATCH] can: rcar_canfd: report the channel number in dev_port

rcar_canfd names its netdevs in probe order, so with only channels 2
and 3 enabled (RZ/V2N on the E1M-X SoMs) channel 2 becomes can0 and
channel 3 becomes can1, and nothing in sysfs says which is which:
dev_id and dev_port both read 0. User space that needs a specific
channel (E1M_X_CAN0 is channel 3 on these SoMs) cannot find it.

Set dev_port to the controller channel, as multi-port Ethernet drivers
do, so /sys/class/net/canN/dev_port names the channel and a udev rule
can match on it.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Alp Lab AB
---
--- a/drivers/net/can/rcar/rcar_canfd.c
+++ b/drivers/net/can/rcar/rcar_canfd.c
@@ -1904,6 +1904,7 @@
 	priv->base = gpriv->base;
 	priv->transceiver = transceiver;
 	priv->channel = ch;
+	ndev->dev_port = ch;
 	priv->gpriv = gpriv;
 	if (transceiver)
 		priv->can.bitrate_max = transceiver->attrs.max_link_rate;
